--
-- **1,494 of them point at one of the nineteen work sequences from seed 0006.**
-- The file says which template each service follows, and those templates are
-- now in the library, so a service that arrives here brings the order the work
-- happens in with it rather than an empty line. The remaining 465 reference
-- templates the task library did not contain — mostly landscaping — and carry
-- no breakdown. They are still worth having as named, CSI-coded services an
-- estimator can build up by hand, and `my_services_without_a_breakdown` lists
-- them so that is a queue rather than a discovery made at bid time.
-- =============================================================================
-- 0007 — The product master
--
-- 1,959 services across 39 trades and 28 CSI divisions, including 59 drone
-- services with their mission and output types — roughly tripling the catalog.
--
-- **What was deliberately left behind: every production rate and every
-- confidence score in the file.** All 2,062 rows carried a rate, and there were
-- nine distinct values among them — 1, 10, 55, 80, 100, 120, 180, 600 — with
-- 828 rows whose rate unit was the word "scope". Against that, the file
-- assigned confidence bands: 1,361 medium-high and 497 high.
--
-- A confidence score is a claim about how well something is known. Importing
-- these would have put "high confidence" on the platform's own placeholders,
-- and RULE-010 exists to stop exactly that. A service that says it has no rate
-- yet is honest and usable; one carrying a fabricated 75% is a trap that only
-- shows up in a bid. The rates come later, from measured production, which is
-- what the calibration machinery is for.
--
-- Three corrections on the way in.
--
-- **42 services appeared twice in the file** — the same work sold under two
-- trades, "Bathtub Installation" under both Bathroom and Plumbing, same CSI
-- code, same unit. One row is kept, preferring the one carrying a CSI code, and
-- the other trade is recorded in the description so nothing is lost.
--
-- **Seven trade names were two spellings of one trade.** "Water Wastewater" and
-- "Water & Wastewater Equipment"; "Material Processing" and "Material
-- Processing & Handling"; "ODOT / Transportation", "Transportation" and
-- "DOT / Transportation". Consolidated, because a picker offering both is a
-- picker that splits a company's own history in half.
--
-- **15 services are priced by the square** — a roofing square is 100 square feet
-- and this schema has no such unit. Converting would change the number, so they
-- are filed lump sum with the original stated in the description rather than
-- silently multiplied by a hundred.
--
-- 47 rows were dropped as services the library already has.
--
-- **Every one gets a cost code, cut by CSI division.** The file carries the
-- division and its title on every row; those become 28 cost codes, and a
-- service rolls up to its division. A service with no cost code cannot reach a
-- budget, which is most of what a service is for once the job is won.
-- =============================================================================



